{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015BFeM1eFW4cguzppaMpK2x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (one package per utility), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build infrastructure, excluded from generation per DD7).\n\n**Implementation state**:\n- Code exists on branch: `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys` (fileinfo), `pkg/format` (color, column, size), `cmd/cat`\n- Specs complete, no code on branch: `cmd/sponge` (rel01.2), `cmd/du` (rel01.3), `cmd/wc` (rel03.0), `cmd/ls` (rel04.0/04.1), `cmd/ts` (rel99.2)\n- Specs pending: true/false/yes/basename/dirname (rel02.0), tee (rel02.1), head/seq (rel02.2)\n\n**Current release**: rel01.2 (sponge) is the earliest incomplete release with complete specs. rel00.0 (infrastructure) and rel01.1 (cat) are effectively complete — their generatable code exists in source.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel00.0 foundational packages all have code. rel01.1 cat has code. The next release is **rel01.2 (sponge)**. Sponge has no dependencies on unbuilt `pkg/` capabilities — it uses only Go standard library I/O. Implementation and tests must be split per P2; proposing the implementation task first per P8.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/sponge implementation -- sponge PRD core requirements (stdin buffering, file write, append mode)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate the sponge PRD -- filename matches prdNNN-sponge.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.2-uc001-sponge.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.2.yaml\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (reference for CLI structure, SIGPIPE handling, error reporting patterns)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component conventions and project structure)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sponge/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"sponge utility: reads all stdin, writes to named output file\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Read all bytes from stdin into memory before writing to any file, per the sponge PRD stdin-buffering requirement\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Write buffered content to the file specified as the positional argument, creating or truncating the file, per the sponge PRD file-write requirement\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Support -a flag for append mode -- open the output file in append mode instead of truncating, per the sponge PRD append-mode requirement\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Handle errors (read failures, write failures, invalid arguments) with messages to stderr and appropriate exit codes per the sponge PRD error-handling requirements\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the CLI patterns established in cmd/cat/main.go: use the flag package for argument parsing, format errors to stderr with the utility name prefix, handle SIGPIPE by exiting cleanly\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Read the sponge PRD found in required_reading and implement every requirement it specifies. The PRD is the authoritative source for all behavior details including flag names, exit codes, edge cases, and stream handling\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/sponge/main.go exists and compiles with go build ./cmd/sponge/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Piping input to sponge writes the complete stdin content to the specified output file\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"The -a flag causes sponge to append to the output file instead of truncating it\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Error conditions produce diagnostic messages on stderr and non-zero exit codes\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"All requirements from the sponge PRD are implemented in cmd/sponge/main.go\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49537,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49537},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcb3d6c7-e86a-43df-a566-720fb90d96fe","uuid":"d63eed8e-7dc1-4e33-8a91-c4dc4aa89fb8"}
